Let $a=⟨1,-3,0⟩$, $b=⟨-2,2,0⟩$ and $c=⟨2,0,-4⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419785 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "20209d26-6af3-5176-8409-17df2aefc0b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419785 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(2\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot 0)\\,-\\,(-3)\\,((-2)\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot 2)\\,+\\,0\\,((-2)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1\\,(-8)\\,-\\,(-3)\\,(8)\\,+\\,0\\,(-4) \\\\  & =-8+24+0 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419788 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419788 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2145564f-b143-5694-829e-a9e30f5dc092" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419788 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186341980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419789 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "69f520c8-2f68-5cc8-8bb4-1d0fcdb03028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419789 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419790 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419790 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7ce27cb2-7851-562f-a805-9613dfe990e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419790 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419791 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419791 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "85680ae8-e720-54c1-a502-614781ce6410" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419791 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419792 #edb/ref 1058 #edb